   - What about `0 < u` in gibbsTerm_step_lt: could weaken to `u ≠ 0`? Hmm, `u ≠ 0` includes negative u. For negative u, `x+u < x` and StrictAnti gives `gibbsTerm c x < gibbsTerm c (x+u)`, so conclusion `gibbsTerm c (x+u) < gibbsTerm c x` is false. So `u > 0` is needed, and `u ≠ 0` fails. Even `0 ≤ u` fails (u=0). Also `0 < u` cannot be weakened to `u > -1` etc.
